  ('723077948995441391', 'Notes for My Son', 2020, 'Drama', 'Fernando Gatti, Santiago Gardinetti, Nayla Zarba', 'Carlos Sorin', 'Valeria Bertuccelli, Esteban Lamothe, Julián Sorín, Mauricio Dayub, Malena Pichot, Catarina Spinetta, Carla Quevedo, Ana Pauls', 'R', 'Battling terminal cancer, a woman writes a one of a kind notebook about life, death and love for her son to remember her by. Based on a true story.', 'Battling terminal cancer, a woman writes a one of a kind notebook about life, death and love for her son to remember her by. Based on a true story.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/nI5XuD0Il8LgsSyPvXESdafAtaD.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:674865'),
  ('452337487103845800', 'Notes from a Women Salesman', 2021, 'Thriller, Drama', 'Fabio Resinaro, Paolo Bellan', 'Fabio Resinaro', 'Mario Sgueglia, Miriam Dalmazio, Libero De Rienzo, Paolo Rossi, Francesco Montanari, Antonio Gerardi, Claudio Bigagli, Michele Placido', null, 'Set in 1978 Milan, Bravo lives his life among luxury clubs and illegal gambling dens in the company of his friend Daytona. Bravo defines himself as an entrepreneur. His business is women - because he sells them. The life of a women salesman is not an easy one, though. The meeting with Carla and a night in the town will change his life forever. Bravo will have to go through his painful past and fight the ultimate battle.', 'Set in 1978 Milan, Bravo lives his life among luxury clubs and illegal gambling dens in the company of his friend Daytona. Bravo defines himself as an entrepreneur. His business is women - because he sells them. The life of a women salesman is not an easy one, though. The meeting with Carla and a night in the town will change his life forever. Bravo will have to go through his painful past and fight the ultimate battle.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/oj5wcSTwYBT838q9zCSIVuhXVTO.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:647740'),
  ('1079242068101572457', 'Notes from Underground', 1995, 'Drama', 'Gary Walkow', 'Gary Walkow', 'Henry Czerny, Sheryl Lee, Jon Favreau, Seth Green', null, 'Adapted from Dostoevsky''s novella, Henry Czerny plays the narrator, Underground Man. Filled with self-hatred, he keeps a video diary where he discusses his own shortcomings and what he thinks is wrong in contemporary society. His bitterness spills over at a dinner party attended by his old college friends, an occasion which sends him running to a nearby brothel, where he meets Liza (Lee), a young prostitute.', 'Adapted from Dostoevsky''s novella, Henry Czerny plays the narrator, Underground Man. Filled with self-hatred, he keeps a video diary where he discusses his own shortcomings and what he thinks is wrong in contemporary society. His bitterness spills over at a dinner party attended by his old college friends, an occasion which sends him running to a nearby brothel, where he meets Liza (Lee), a young prostitute.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/hsIsNGLElvJNUSi33hqD7CdVhFx.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:106603'),
  ('974524696118928341', 'Notes on a Scandal', 2006, 'Drama, Romance', 'Richard Eyre, Chris Menges, Jane Harwood', 'Patrick Marber', 'Judi Dench, Cate Blanchett, Bill Nighy, Andrew Simpson, Phil Davis, Michael Maloney, Juno Temple, Max Lewis', 'R', 'A veteran high school teacher befriends a younger art teacher, who is having an affair with one of her 15-year-old students. However, her intentions with this new "friend" also go well beyond platonic friendship.', 'A veteran high school teacher befriends a younger art teacher, who is having an affair with one of her 15-year-old students. However, her intentions with this new "friend" also go well beyond platonic friendship.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/ieX6ZO2Kf2qjoIBXbQW5awivbhY.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:1259'),
  ('360869882141073146', 'Notes on a True Story', 1951, 'Documentary', 'Luchino Visconti, Domenico Scala', 'Vasco Pratolini', 'Vasco Pratolini', null, 'On the evening of March 11, 1950, Annabella Bracci, a 12-year-old girl, was brutally killed and thrown into a pit on the outskirts of Rome, near the village of Primavalle. A brief and poetic account of the events and their impact on an impoverished community. A handful of wild flowers and a painful catch in the voices.', 'On the evening of March 11, 1950, Annabella Bracci, a 12-year-old girl, was brutally killed and thrown into a pit on the outskirts of Rome, near the village of Primavalle. A brief and poetic account of the events and their impact on an impoverished community. A handful of wild flowers and a painful catch in the voices.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/tKEkw2AaL9Y0ZhkxUOxpvrYojbY.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:297757'),
  ('15005655120298957', 'Notes on Blindness', 2016, 'Drama, Documentary', 'Gerry Floyd, James Spinney, Amaya Valentina Gonzalez Perez', 'James Spinney, Pete Middleton', 'John M. Hull, Marilyn Hull, Dan Renton Skinner, Simone Kirby, Eileen Davies, David Hobbs, Victoria Wicks, Jamie Bradley', null, 'After losing sight in 1983, John Hull began keeping an audio diary, a unique testimony of loss, rebirth and renewal, excavating the interior world of blindness. Following on from the Emmy Award-winning short film of the same name, Notes on Blindness is an ambitious and groundbreaking work, both affecting and innovative.', 'After losing sight in 1983, John Hull began keeping an audio diary, a unique testimony of loss, rebirth and renewal, excavating the interior world of blindness. Following on from the Emmy Award-winning short film of the same name, Notes on Blindness is an ambitious and groundbreaking work, both affecting and innovative.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/y4vc2bbd3VJDcld7iUg5v0kYU3q.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:378441'),
  ('1010043639027742700', 'Notes on the Circus', 1967, 'Documentary', 'Jonas Mekas', null, null, null, 'Jonas Mekas transforms footage of the Ringling Brothers Circus into a rapid-fire montage set to music, structured in four segments that highlight different acts. Earlier images reappear in later sections as background to new performances, with the accelerated pacing of the clips mirroring the rhythm and energy of the soundtrack.', 'Jonas Mekas transforms footage of the Ringling Brothers Circus into a rapid-fire montage set to music, structured in four segments that highlight different acts. Earlier images reappear in later sections as background to new performances, with the accelerated pacing of the clips mirroring the rhythm and energy of the soundtrack.', 'https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/kvEhxB2kVUgoNm1LTastVr8EpTh.jpg', 'tmdb:movie:238623'),
